        "title": "Computer Vision - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Computer graphics answers a *forward* question: given a 3D scene and a camera, what\npixels result? Computer vision answers the *inverse* question: given the pixels, what\nscene produced them? That inversion is ill-posed — infinitely many scenes project to\nthe same image — so every method in this directory is, at root, a way of injecting the\npriors and constraints that pick out the *one* scene we actually care about."
    }
